  "limitations": [
    "The 600-step reference comparison covers 10 simulated seconds of hold, withdrawal, advancement and settling from the saved long-tool state; not the complete manual crossover.",
    "Browser runs cover 300 steps with a lightweight preview, not the full fluoroscopic renderer and app idle scheduler.",
    "The local mesh threshold is not a global guarantee: every accepted step is compared against the full model at all polygonal breakpoints.",
    "Early contact recovery can change internal temporal subdivision; outer dt remains 1/60 s and all original physical acceptance thresholds are retained.",
    "The ordinary adaptive application factory has different historical solver defaults; any future application integration must explicitly preserve the strict tolerances used here."
  ],
  "nextWork": [
    "Use mesh plus early contact recovery as the candidate for further measurements; neither pruning alone nor increasingly coarse mesh reliably removes expensive tails.",
    "Profile the combined candidate and test the full app scheduler; current browser physics remains 43.1 Hz despite CPU-only average 62.4 steps/s.",
    "Verify longer motion and rotation sequences and the complete crossover before enabling the approximation by default."
  ]
